      "content": "Start by checking your thermostat settings to ensure the room temperature is actually being set lower than the current bedroom temperature and that the system isn't in \"fan only\" mode, which circulates warm air but doesn't cool it. You can also try gently pulling the handles of the bedroom's specific air vent registers; if they don't wiggle freely, mechanical damage or sticking rollers may be blocking airflow. Finally, feel the vents in that bedroom to confirm they truly feel cool while you touch nearby, unaffected vents to see if the thermostat is actually sending cold air to the house at all.",
